# `plat`'s own root file. `plat` is a plain, ordinary `--extern` package --
# unlike `core`, it gets no ambient-prelude or `for`-block privilege, and no
# eager-discovery exemption of its own; it's just a package that happens to
# ship `@glue` implementations for `core`'s gaps (see `core::glue` and
# docs/21-gaps-and-glue.md). Its own local build is still eager regardless
# of import (every package's is, see docs/10-modules-and-linkage.md), so
# nothing here needs to import a platform submodule for it to be part of
# the build or for a consumer to discover its glue. This file has nothing
# left to declare; it exists only because the compiler still needs a
# conventionally-named entry file to find (`plat.omg`/`plat/plat.omg`)
# when `plat` itself is compiled standalone (`just build-plat`).
#
# Each platform `plat` ships lives in its own nested module (`plat::libc`
# today; a future `plat::windows`/`plat::wasm` would be a sibling) --
# there is no selection mechanism between them yet, since this compiler
# has no target/OS conditional-compilation concept at all. `libc` is
# simply the one platform that exists right now, not a chosen default
# among several.
